n Spray BSbase1-73 Your opponent shuffles his or her hand into his or her deck, then draws 7 cards.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/73.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/73_hires.png2Impostor Professor Oak BSbase1-74Item FinderâDiscard 2 of the other cards from your hand in order to put a Trainer card from your discard pile into your hand.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/74.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/74_hires.pngItem Finder BSbase1-75LassêYou and your opponent show each other your hands, then shuffle all the Trainer cards from your hands into your decks.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/75.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/75_hires.pngLass BSbase1-76Pokémon Breeder¾Put a Stage 2 Evolution card from your hand on the matching Basic Pokémon. You can only play this card when you would be allowed to evolve that Pokémon anyway.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/76.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/76_hires.png$Pokémon Breeder BSbase1-77Pokémon TraderòTrade 1 of the Basic Pokémon or Evolution cards in your hand for 1 of the Basic Pokémon or Evolution cards from your deck. Show both cards to your opponent. Shuffle your deck afterward.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/77.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/77_hires.png"Pokémon Trader BSbase1-78Scoop UpöChoose 1 of your Pokémon in play and return its Basic Pokémon card to your hand. (Discard all cards attached to that card.)Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/78.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/78_hires.pngScoop Up BSbase1-79(Super Energy RemovalĞDiscard 1 Energy card attached to 1 of your Pokémon in order to choose 1 of your opponent's Pokémon and up to 2 Energy cards attached to it. Discard those Energy cards.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/79.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/79_hires.png.Super Energy Removal BSbase1-80Defender„Attach Defender to 1 of your Pokémon. At the end of your opponent's next turn, discard Defender. Damage done to that Pokémon by attacks is reduced by 20 (after applying Weakness and Resistance).Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/80.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/80_hires.pngDefender BSbase1-81 Energy Retrieval¼Trade 1 of the other cards in your hand for up to 2 basic Energy cards from your discard pile.standardRhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/81.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/81_hires.png&Energy Retrieval BSbase1-82Full Heal”Your Active Pokémon is no longer Asleep, Confused, Paralyzed, or Poisoned.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/82.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/82_hires.pngFull Heal BSbase1-83Maintenance¦Shuffle 2 of the other cards from your hand into your deck in order to draw a card.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/83.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/83_hires.pngMaintenance BSbase1-84PlusPowerêAttach PlusPower to your Active Pokémon. At the end of your turn, discard PlusPower. If this Pokémon's attack does damage to the Defending Pokémon (after applying Weakness and Resistance), the attack does 10 more damage to the Defending Pokémon.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/84.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/84_hires.pngPlusPower BSbase1-85Pokémon CenterœRemove all damage counters from all of your own Pokémon with damage counters on them, then discard all Energy cards attached to those Pokémon.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/85.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/85_hires.png"Pokémon Center BSbase1-86Pokémon FluteÀChoose 1 Basic Pokémon card from your opponent's discard pile and put it onto his or her Bench. (You can't play Pokémon Flute if your opponent's Bench is full.)Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/86.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/86_hires.png Pokemon Flute BSbase1-87PokédexLook at up to 5 cards from the top of your deck and rearrange them as you like.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/87.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/87_hires.pngPokedex BSbase1-88Professor OakJDiscard your hand, then draw 7 cards.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/88.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/88_hires.png Professor Oak BSbase1-89Revive”Put 1 Basic Pokémon card from your discard pile onto your Bench. Put damage counters on that Pokémon equal to half its HP (rounded down to the nearest 10). (You can't play Revive if your Bench is full.)Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/89.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/89_hires.pngRevive BSbase1-90Super PotionàDiscard 1 Energy card attached to your own Pokémon in order to remove up to 4 damage counters from that Pokémon.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/90.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/90_hires.pngSuper Potion BSbase1-91BillDraw 2 cards.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/91.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/91_hires.pngBill BSbase1-92Energy RemovalšChoose 1 Energy card attached to 1 of your opponent's Pokémon and discard it.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/92.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/92_hires.png"Energy Removal BSbase1-93Gust of Wind²Choose 1 of your opponent's Benched Pokémon and switch it with his or her Active Pokémon.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/93.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/93_hires.pngGust of Wind BSbase1-94PotionlRemove up to 2 damage counters from 1 of your Pokémon.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/94.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/94_hires.pngPotion BSbase1-95Switch|Switch 1 of your own Benched Pokémon with your Active Pokémon.Rhttps://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/95.png^https://images.pokemontcg.io/base1/95_hires.pngSwitch BSbase1-96.Double Colorless EnergyEnergySpecial’Provides ColorlessColorless energy.
